  "about": {
    "title": "How the Arbiter Works",
    "body": "The Arbiter periodically queries the Producer and Consumer APIs to compare which messages were sent versus which were received. It fetches the most recent message sequences from the Producer (sent list) and asks the Consumer which sequences are missing from its database. Any gap is recorded as an audit entry. The reconcile interval controls how often this comparison runs (default: every 10 seconds). High Consumer Lag or missing sequences indicate delivery problems — check Kafka connectivity and consumer throughput first."
  },
